# Docker & Kubernetes Deployment

For Minikube: Run eval $(minikube docker-env) before building images.

## Dockerization

Build Docker images for the backend and frontend:

```bash
# Backend
    docker build -t <name>-event-backend:latest .

# Frontend
    docker build -t <name>-event-frontend:latest .

# Check the images
    docker images

Kubernetes Deployment
    1. Ensure your Kubernetes cluster can access local Docker images.
        For Docker Desktop: Images are available by default.
        

    2. Apply the Kubernetes manifests:
    ```bash
        kubectl apply -f k8s/backend-deployment.yaml
        kubectl apply -f k8s/frontend-deployment.yaml
        kubectl apply -f k8s/mysql.yaml
        kubectl apply -f k8s/ingress.yaml
    ```
    3. Verify the deployments and services:
    ```bash
        kubectl get pods
        kubectl get svc
        kubectl get ingress
    ```


